/*
	Since
		y ^ x = y % x > x,
	MSB of y and x must be the same.
	Then, y - x < x, and thus
		y % x = y - x,
	which means (y & x) = x.
	Hence, the answer equals to the number of pairs (x, y) such that
		L <= x <= y <= R,
		(MSB of x) = (MSB of y),
		for all i, [i-th bit of x is 1 => that of y is also 1].
*/

